<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n7267" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Căystrŏs</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-us</span></b> , i, m.,
		= <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κάϋστρος</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a river in Lydia</i>, <i>which rises in Mount Tmolus</i>, <i>and falls
				into the sea at Ephesus</i>, celebrated for the great number of
			its swans, now <i>Kara - Su</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Caystros,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					5, 386</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Mel. 1, 17, 2</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Caystrus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Q. N. 4, 2, 19</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Verg. G. 1, 384</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Prop. 3</span></i>
			(4), 22, 15; <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 2, 253</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 5, 29,
				31, § 115</span></i>.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Căy-strĭus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj., <i>of Caystros</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ales = cygnus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					Tr. 5, 1, 11</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
